      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-0",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Scheduled bean methods"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-0-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@EnableScheduling",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " enables Spring\u2019s processing of "
        ],
        [
          "@Scheduled",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " methods."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-0-note-0-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "It belongs on a scanned configuration class."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-0-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@Scheduled",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " supplies the timing rule on a bean method."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-0-note-1-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring registers the method with a scheduler when it creates the application context."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-0-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A regular scheduled method takes no arguments."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-0-note-2-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring calls it without a controller request and ignores its return value."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-0-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The method must belong to a Spring bean."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-0-note-3-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Creating the class with "
        ],
        [
          "new",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " does not register its scheduled methods."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-1",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Timing rules"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-1-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "fixedDelay",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " waits after the previous run finishes."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-1-note-0-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "fixedRate",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " schedules starts at a fixed interval."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-1-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A busy scheduler can start work late."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-1-note-1-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "fixedRate",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " does not promise parallel executions of a single periodic task."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-1-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "cron",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " expresses a calendar rule."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-1-note-2-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring uses six fields: second, minute, hour, day of month, month, day of week."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-1-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "zone",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " selects the timezone for a cron rule."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-1-note-3-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Without it, the scheduler\u2019s timezone applies."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-1-example-0",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Run a weekly method",
        "language": "java",
        "description": [
          "Each tab names a file relative to the project root. Java `17` and Maven are required. `mvn spring-boot:run` starts this example after its external requirements are configured.",
          "The project uses Spring Boot 3.5 and `spring-boot-starter`.",
          "The web starter already includes that base starter.",
          "`WeeklyJob.java` belongs in `src/main/java/com/example/demo`, in the scanned package.",
          "The application stays running until Sunday at `09:00` in `Asia/Kolkata`.",
          "The method does not run immediately on startup.",
          "The example logs one line to make scheduling visible.",
          "The next lesson supplies a concrete digest operation."
        ],
        "code": "",
        "explanation": [
          "`@EnableScheduling` activates registration.",
          "`@Component` makes `WeeklyJob` eligible for that registration.",
          "The cron fields `0 0 9 * * SUN` select Sunday at `09:00:00`.",
          "Spring calls `run` at that time.",
          "The method itself does not calculate the next run.",
          "For an interval case, `@Scheduled(fixedDelay = 60000)` instead waits `60000` milliseconds after completion.",
          "It replaces the cron annotation."
        ],
        "result": "Weekly job started",
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/WeeklyJob.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.slf4j.Logger;\nimport org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;\nimport org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;\nimport org.springframework.scheduling.annotation.EnableScheduling;\nimport org.springframework.scheduling.annotation.Scheduled;\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Component;\n\n@Component\nclass WeeklyJob {\n    private static final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(WeeklyJob.class);\n\n    @Scheduled(cron = \"0 0 9 * * SUN\", zone = \"Asia/Kolkata\")\n    void run() {\n        log.info(\"Weekly job started\");\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/SchedulingConfiguration.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.slf4j.Logger;\nimport org.slf4j.LoggerFactory;\nimport org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;\nimport org.springframework.scheduling.annotation.EnableScheduling;\nimport org.springframework.scheduling.annotation.Scheduled;\nimport org.springframework.stereotype.Component;\n\n@Configuration\n@EnableScheduling\nclass SchedulingConfiguration {}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/DemoApplication.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class DemoApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "pom.xml",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd\">\n    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n    <parent>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n        <version>3.5.16</version>\n        <relativePath/>\n    </parent>\n    <groupId>com.example</groupId>\n    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.0</version>\n    <properties><java.version>17</java.version></properties>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n    <build>\n        <finalName>demo</finalName>\n        <plugins>\n            <plugin>\n                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>\n            </plugin>\n        </plugins>\n    </build>\n\n</project>\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Execution and restart limits"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Ordinary Boot scheduling uses one scheduler thread by default when virtual-thread scheduling is not enabled."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2-note-0-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A long task can delay other scheduled tasks."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "spring.task.scheduling.pool.size",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " can enlarge a pooled scheduler."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2-note-1-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Thread count does not coordinate separate application instances."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Each application instance registers its own scheduled methods."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2-note-2-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Two instances can perform the same weekly work."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A shared lock or a dedicated scheduler can limit concurrent startup."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2-note-3-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A unique job-and-period record can identify duplicate work."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2-note-4",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "@Scheduled",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " does not save job history or replay missed runs."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2-note-4-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Durable pending work and retry state need separate storage."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2-note-5",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A failure in one recurring run does not by itself create a durable retry."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations-scheduling-lesson-2-note-5-part-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Database and provider calls still need timeouts and recorded failure handling."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
